<title>ARGENTINA: Argentine Dec car output rises 179.5 pct vs 95.</title>
<headline>Argentine Dec car output rises 179.5 pct vs 95.</headline>
<dateline>BUENOS AIRES 1997-02-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Argentine auto production in January was 179.5 percent higher than the same month last year at 12,909 units, but fell 49.8 percent versus a month earlier, the industry lobby ADEFA said Thursday.</p>
<p>&quot;This month's figures are influenced by the annual vacation period,&quot; ADEFA said in a statement.</p>
<p>Domestic car sales reached 23,818, an increase of 13.9 percent on January 1995 and down 45 percent from December.</p>
<p>Exports for the month surged 421.8 percent from the same month last year to 6,110, which was 27.2 percent lower than the previous month.</p>
<p>((--Axel Bugge, Buenos Aires Newsroom, 541 318-0668))</p>
